  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 134 PM CDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\nMid-level high pressure continues, of course, but there is the \npotential for slightly more interesting things happening at the \nsurface. Low rain (15-25%) chances will return Monday as PWAT values \nreach 1.7-2.0\" and outflow boundaries from storms to the north move \ntoward the coast, colliding with the seabreeze. Low rain chances \nwill continue along the seabreeze Tuesday. \n\nThe NBM continues to indicate PoP values in the 20-50% range \nbeginning Wednesday but, as the previous forecast mentioned, based \non global models and understanding the NBM bias, expect these will \ncontinue to trend drier. South of the area, more moisture will \nresult in higher rainfall totals. The NBM may be picking up on this \nand nudging it a little too far north. Either way, we'll keep an eye \non this and update the forecast as needed.",
